  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Find the ratios $\\dfrac{a_2}{a_1}$ and $\\dfrac{a_3}{a_2}$ for each sequence to test whether it is a GP.\n\nIf the sequence is a GP, write down the first term $a$ and the common ratio $r$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$4,8,16,\\ldots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "GP: $a=4$, $r=2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a_2}{a_1}&=\\frac{8}{4}=2\\\\\\frac{a_3}{a_2}&=\\frac{16}{8}=2\\end{aligned}$$\nThe ratios are equal, so it is a GP with $a=4$ and $r=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$16,8,4,\\ldots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "GP: $a=16$, $r=\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a_2}{a_1}&=\\frac{8}{16}=\\frac12\\\\\\frac{a_3}{a_2}&=\\frac{4}{8}=\\frac12\\end{aligned}$$\nThe ratios are equal, so it is a GP with $a=16$ and $r=\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2,4,6,\\ldots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not a GP.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a_2}{a_1}&=\\frac{4}{2}=2\\\\\\frac{a_3}{a_2}&=\\frac{6}{4}=\\frac32\\end{aligned}$$\nThe ratios are different, so it is not a GP.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$-1000,-100,-10,\\ldots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "GP: $a=-1000$, $r=\\dfrac1{10}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a_2}{a_1}&=\\frac{-100}{-1000}=\\frac1{10}\\\\\\frac{a_3}{a_2}&=\\frac{-10}{-100}=\\frac1{10}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe ratios are equal, so it is a GP with $a=-1000$ and $r=\\frac1{10}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$-80,40,-20,\\ldots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "GP: $a=-80$, $r=-\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a_2}{a_1}&=\\frac{40}{-80}=-\\frac12\\\\\\frac{a_3}{a_2}&=\\frac{-20}{40}=-\\frac12\\end{aligned}$$\nThe ratios are equal, so it is a GP with $a=-80$ and $r=-\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
